<title>CANADA: Quebecor Printing buys printing facility.</title>
<headline>Quebecor Printing buys printing facility.</headline>
<dateline>MONTREAL 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quebecor Printing Inc said on Thursday that its U.S. subsidiary agreed with McGraw-Hill Cos to buy the William C. Brown printing facility in Dubuque, Iowa.</p>
<p>Financial terms were not disclosed.  </p>
<p>The printing operations include book printing and short-run facilities that specialize in the professional and textbook markets and employ about 250 people.</p>
<p>The acquisition was conditional on the completion of a transaction involving printing assets that McGraw-Hill is acquiring as part of its purchase of five Times Mirror Higher Education business units, Quebecor Printing said.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Montreal bureau (514) 985-2434</p>
</text>
